# BrandForge — Semrush enrichment (optional). Two ways to connect; pick ONE.
# With neither configured the app runs fine, just without live search data.

# ── Option A: Analytics REST API ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Classic API key. Requires a Semrush plan with API units (usually the
# separate API add-on). Simplest setup: paste the key, done.
SEMRUSH_API_KEY=

# ── Option B: Semrush MCP server ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Uses Semrush's official MCP endpoint (https://mcp.semrush.com/v2/mcp).
# Included with Semrush One Starter/Pro+ and SEO Classic Pro/Guru plans
# (50K API units) — no separate API add-on purchase. See
# https://www.semrush.com/mcp-access for plan details.
#
# B1. OAuth (default): set SEMRUSH_MODE=mcp, start the app, then click
#     "Connect Semrush account" in the Insights step (or open
#     /api/semrush/connect). Tokens persist in data/semrush-oauth.json.
# B2. API key over MCP: additionally set SEMRUSH_MCP_API_KEY and skip OAuth.
#SEMRUSH_MODE=mcp
#SEMRUSH_MCP_API_KEY=

# ── Advanced overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SEMRUSH_MODE=api|mcp        force a backend (default: api if key set, else mcp if connected)
# SEMRUSH_DATABASE=us         regional database
# SEMRUSH_MCP_URL=            override MCP endpoint (testing)
# SEMRUSH_API_URL=            override REST endpoint (testing)
# SEMRUSH_MCP_REDIRECT_URL=   public OAuth callback URL when behind a proxy/domain,
#                             e.g. https://yourapp.com/api/semrush/callback
# PORT=3000
